# Rule authoring

Prefer: `description` and/or `globs`; `alwaysApply: false` unless ≤~40 lines and must load every turn. Never put triple-dash fences inside `.mdc` body examples (breaks parsers).

Avoid: fat alwaysApply; 20+ line pasted samples (use `@path`); `.cursorrules`; duplicating into AGENTS+CLAUDE+.mdc; procedures → skills instead.

Shape: under 50 lines; one concern; bullets. Model hints belong in one lean always-on rule, not every file.
